      "text_raw": "On the total schematic, the\nfour output transistors with\ntheir amplifier, are easily\nrecognized. The amplifier\nis shown with unity-gain\nfeedback.\nActually, this is a three-\nstage amplifier. The input\nstage is a folded cascode.\nDistributed Miller compen-\nsation is applied however,\nnot nested Miller. This\nmethod of compensation is\nmuch less transparent.\nThe CMFB amplifier is in\nthe middle, with M20/M21\nand R2/R3.",
      "text": "On the total schematic, the four output transistors with their amplifier, are easily recognized. The amplifier is shown with unity-gain feedback. Actually, this is a threestage amplifier. The input stage is a folded cascode. Distributed Miller compensation is applied however, not nested Miller. This method of compensation is much less transparent. The CMFB amplifier is in the middle, with M20/M21 and R2/R3."
    }
